cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  driftwatch: conjunction screening on public element sets, with a measured
  storm-term calibration
message: >-
  Citation metadata for driftwatch and the tagged Swarm calibration benchmark.
  The benchmark compares public element sets with ESA's precise science orbits.
  The release identifies the frozen measurements and their bounded population.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pather
    given-names: Nikhil
repository-code: "https://github.com/nikhilb9244-cloud/driftwatch"
abstract: >-
  driftwatch screens a fleet against the public catalogue, estimates collision
  probability with an uncertainty model fitted from how successive element sets
  for the same object disagree, and adds a storm term that displaces objects and
  widens their covariance under a geomagnetic scenario. Its storm term and its
  covariance are calibrated against ESA's reduced-dynamic precise science orbits
  for Swarm A, B and C over three windows: a quiet control, the May 2024 Gannon
  storm, and a held-out October 2024 window. Positions come from public element
  sets, published predictions or supplied orbit products; the project performs no orbit determination of its own, and every
  probability it reports is indicative rather than operational.
keywords:
  - conjunction assessment
  - space situational awareness
  - SGP4
  - geomagnetic storm
  - thermospheric drag
  - orbit uncertainty
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-07"
references:
  - type: data
    title: Swarm Level 2 precise science orbits (SW_OPER_SP3xCOM_2_)
    authors:
      - name: European Space Agency
    url: "https://swarm-diss.eo.esa.int/"
    notes: >-
      Reduced-dynamic reconstructed orbits, used as the independent reference in
      the calibration benchmark. Epochs are GPS time and are converted to UTC.
  - type: data
    title: Swarm Level 1b spacecraft dynamics (SW_OPER_SC_xDYN_1B)
    authors:
      - name: European Space Agency
    url: "https://swarm-diss.eo.esa.int/"
    notes: >-
      The published thruster record, used to decide which intervals contain a
      manoeuvre rather than inferring one from a residual.
  - type: data
    title: General perturbations element sets
    authors:
      - name: United States Space Force
      - name: Space-Track.org
    url: "https://www.space-track.org/"
    notes: >-
      Element sets and gp_history, redistributed with citation under Space-Track's
      user agreement.
  - type: data
    title: General perturbations element sets and space weather indices
    authors:
      - name: CelesTrak
    url: "https://celestrak.org/"
  - type: data
    title: Geomagnetic and solar indices
    authors:
      - name: NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center
    url: "https://services.swpc.noaa.gov/"
